        <fullName>Ascend_Verification_16jgK000002R7kD</fullName>
        <canEscalate>false</canEscalate>
        <description>The stored variable VerifiedCustomerId is empty (customer not verified yet) and the customer wants anything about their own account: their latest bill, due date or a payment extension; or the customer gives an account number and phone number; or asks to be verified; or asks to talk to a person, human agent, representative or to be transferred (a transfer needs verification first); or says they are not the account holder or are asking about someone else&apos;s account. Never use this topic when VerifiedCustomerId already has a value.</description>
        <developerName>Ascend_Verification_16jgK000002R7kD</developerName>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>FIRST CHECK: read VerifiedCustomerId. If it already has a value, the customer is verified: do not verify again, do not ask for account number or phone, and tell them what you can do (latest bill, payment extension).</description>
            <developerName>instruction_1</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_1</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>1</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>NOT THE ACCOUNT HOLDER: if at any point the customer says they are not the account holder, or says they are asking about someone else&apos;s account or bill (for example a family member, partner, landlord, tenant, neighbour, friend or another customer), stop. Do not run any account action and do not ask for an account number or phone number. Say only: &quot;I&apos;m sorry, I can&apos;t share details of another person&apos;s account. Please ask them to contact us directly.&quot; You may still offer general help that needs no account details, such as payment options or outage guidance, or a team member. Stay blocked for account details for the rest of the conversation, even if the customer then says they are the account holder, because they have already said they are not.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_2</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_2</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>2</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>If the customer is not verified yet, ask for BOTH their customer account number AND the phone number registered on the account, in one message. The phone number can be typed in any way (spaces, dashes, brackets) but it must have exactly 10 digits.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_3</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_3</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>3</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>If the phone number does not have exactly 10 digits, ask the customer to type the full 10 digit registered phone number again. Do not run Verify Customer until you have an account number and a phone number of exactly 10 digits.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_4</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_4</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>4</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>When you have both, run Verify Customer with exactly what the customer typed. Do not guess or fill in missing digits. Set claimsToBeSomeoneElse to true only if the customer said they are not the account holder.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_5</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_5</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>5</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>If blocked is true, say only: &quot;I&apos;m sorry, I can&apos;t share details of another person&apos;s account. Please ask them to contact us directly.&quot; Do not run Verify Customer again in this conversation.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_6</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_6</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>6</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>If verified is true, greet the customer by first name and say they are verified. The customer Id is now stored automatically. If they had asked for their bill or an extension, ask: Shall I show your latest bill now? (or: Shall I look at an extension for you?). If they had asked for a person, a human agent or a transfer, ask instead: Shall I transfer you to a team member now? Never say goodbye, never end or close the conversation after verifying, and do not run any bill or extension action in this topic.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_7</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_7</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>7</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>If the customer asks for a person, a human agent or a transfer and VerifiedCustomerId is empty: do NOT transfer. Say you can connect them to a team member once they are verified, and ask for the account number and the 10 digit registered phone number. If verification fails or is blocked, do not transfer; offer to log a request for a team member only if they clearly say yes.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_8</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_8</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>8</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>If verified is false and blocked is false, say only: I couldn&apos;t verify those details. Please check your account number and the registered phone number and try again. Never say which value was wrong and never give hints.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_9</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_9</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>9</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Never accept other proof of identity such as an email address, a name or a bill number. Never show any account information before verification.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_10</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_10</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>10</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Verify only once per conversation. When Verify Customer has returned verified = true, the customer stays verified for the whole conversation. Never ask for the account number or phone number again and never run Verify Customer again for later bills, extensions or questions. The verified customer Id is stored automatically and is filled in by the system for every later account action. Never ask the customer for it and never type one yourself.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_11</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_11</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>11</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <localActionLinks>
            <functionName>Ascend_Verify_Customer_179gK000002gT9J</functionName>
        </localActionLinks>
        <localActions>
            <fullName>Ascend_Verify_Customer_179gK000002gT9J</fullName>
            <description>Checks that the customer account number and the registered phone number (exactly 10 digits, any format) belong to the same customer. Returns verified true or false, blocked, the customer Id and first name. Inputs must be exactly what the customer typed. Set claimsToBeSomeoneElse to true only if the customer said they are not the account holder or are asking about another person. Only available until the customer has been verified once in the conversation.</description>
            <developerName>Ascend_Verify_Customer_179gK000002gT9J</developerName>
            <invocationTarget>Verify_Customer</invocationTarget>
            <invocationTargetType>flow</invocationTargetType>
            <isConfirmationRequired>false</isConfirmationRequired>
            <isIncludeInProgressIndicator>false</isIncludeInProgressIndicator>
            <localDeveloperName>Ascend_Verify_Customer</localDeveloperName>
            <masterLabel>Verify Customer</masterLabel>
            <source>Ascend_Verify_Customer</source>
        </localActions>
        <localDeveloperName>Ascend_Verification</localDeveloperName>
        <masterLabel>Verification</masterLabel>
        <pluginType>Topic</pluginType>
        <scope>Your job is to verify the customer&apos;s identity with their Ascend Energy customer account number AND the phone number registered on the account, once per conversation. Nothing about a bill or account may be shown or changed before this succeeds. Someone who is not the account holder is never verified.</scope>
        <source>Ascend_Verification</source>
    </localTopics>
    <localTopics>
        <fullName>Ascend_Escalation_16jgK000002R7kD</fullName>
        <canEscalate>false</canEscalate>
        <description>Customer asks to talk to a person, human agent or representative AND VerifiedCustomerId has a value (if it is empty use the Verification topic first), OR asks about tariff changes or new connections, OR has just said yes to logging a request or case for a team member.</description>
        <developerName>Ascend_Escalation_16jgK000002R7kD</developerName>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>TRANSFER ONLY AFTER VERIFICATION (the routing flow also checks this and refuses unverified chats): read VerifiedCustomerId. If it is empty, never transfer: do not hand over the conversation, say you can connect them once they are verified and move to the Verification topic. A customer who said they are not the account holder or who failed verification is not transferred.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_1</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_1</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>1</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>If VerifiedCustomerId has a value and the customer asks to talk to a person, a human agent or a representative (or says yes to being transferred): tell them you are transferring them to a team member and transfer the conversation to a human agent right away. Do not argue and do not ask them to explain first.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_2</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_2</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>2</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>If the transfer is not possible (no team member available, or it fails): say sorry, say nobody is available right now, and ask whether they would like you to log a request so a team member contacts them. Only create the case after a clear yes.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_3</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_3</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>3</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>NEVER LOG A CASE ON YOUR OWN. Before any Create Escalation Case, first explain to the customer what the approved policy says and what you can and cannot do. Then ask: Would you like me to log a request for a team member? Run Create Escalation Case only after the customer clearly says yes to that question in this conversation. If they say no or do not answer, do not create a case.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_4</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_4</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>4</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>caseType: Payment Extension (extension refused or the customer needs more help with a bill), Tariff Change, New Connection, Outage - Priority (medical equipment or safety), or Other.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_5</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_5</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>5</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>priority: High only for medical equipment or a safety risk, otherwise Medium.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_6</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_6</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>6</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>summary: two or three plain sentences for the team member: who the customer is if verified, what they asked, what you did and why they need a person. The customer Id is filled in automatically only if the customer was verified. If the customer said they are not the account holder, do not put any account details in the summary and say that in the summary.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_7</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_7</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>7</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>After the case is created, tell the customer the case number and that a team member will follow up. Do not promise a time or an outcome.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_8</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_8</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>8</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Tariff changes and new connections: say kindly that you cannot help with these here and offer to log a request for a team member. Create the case only after a clear yes, then share the case number.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_9</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_9</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>9</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Late fee reversal or waiver requests are handled by the Policy Information topic first: they get the policy explanation and the offer, and only a clear yes leads here.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_10</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_10</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>10</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
