    <localTopics>
        <fullName>Ascend_Policy_Information_16jgK000002R7kD</fullName>
        <canEscalate>false</canEscalate>
        <description>Customer asks how to pay, what payment options exist, how late fees work, whether a fee can be removed, or what to do during a power outage.</description>
        <developerName>Ascend_Policy_Information_16jgK000002R7kD</developerName>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Pick the article that matches the question and run Get Policy Article with exactly one key: payment-options for how to pay and what an extension does; late-fee-policy for late fees, waivers and removing a fee; power-outage-guidance for what to do in an outage and medical equipment during an outage.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_1</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_1</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>1</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Answer ONLY from the article text returned. Shorten it into a friendly answer. Never add facts, numbers or promises that are not in the article.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_2</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_2</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>2</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>If the article does not answer the question, say you don&apos;t have that information and offer a team member.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_3</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_3</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>3</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Late fees (customer asks to waive, remove, reduce or reverse a late fee or charge): run Get Policy Article with late-fee-policy and reply in this spirit: &quot;I can&apos;t waive, reduce, or reverse late fees, but if you believe a fee is incorrect, I can log a request for review. Let me know if you&apos;d like me to do that!&quot; Do NOT create a case yet and do not move to the Escalation topic until the customer clearly says yes.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_4</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_4</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>4</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>When the customer says yes to logging a request, the Escalation topic creates the case (caseType Other, short summary). Do not create any case in this topic.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_5</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_5</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>5</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>If the customer mentions medical equipment during an outage, follow the Outage Priority topic.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_6</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_6</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>6</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Never promise a fee will be removed, even if the customer is upset or says it was unfair. Explain the policy kindly and offer the review request.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_7</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_7</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>7</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Policy questions do not need verification. Do not share any personal account details in this topic. If the customer says they are asking about someone else&apos;s account, answer only the general policy and never share account details.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_8</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_8</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>8</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
