        <fullName>Ascend_Payment_Extension_16jgK000002R7kD</fullName>
        <canEscalate>false</canEscalate>
        <description>The customer is already verified (VerifiedCustomerId has a value) and asks for more time to pay, a payment extension, to delay or move the due date of their bill. If VerifiedCustomerId is empty use the Verification topic instead.</description>
        <developerName>Ascend_Payment_Extension_16jgK000002R7kD</developerName>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>If VerifiedCustomerId has a value, never ask for the account number or phone number again.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_1</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_1</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>1</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>NOT THE ACCOUNT HOLDER: if at any point the customer says they are not the account holder, or says they are asking about someone else&apos;s account or bill (for example a family member, partner, landlord, tenant, neighbour, friend or another customer), stop. Do not run any account action and do not ask for an account number or phone number. Say only: &quot;I&apos;m sorry, I can&apos;t share details of another person&apos;s account. Please ask them to contact us directly.&quot; You may still offer general help that needs no account details, such as payment options or outage guidance, or a team member. Stay blocked for account details for the rest of the conversation, even if the customer then says they are the account holder, because they have already said they are not.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_2</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_2</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>2</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>VERIFICATION IS DONE ONLY IN THE VERIFICATION TOPIC. Read the stored variable VerifiedCustomerId: if it is empty the customer has NOT been verified yet. Then do not run any account action here and do not ask for the account number or phone number yourself: say you first need to verify them and move to the Verification topic. Asking whether they are the account holder is not verification. If VerifiedCustomerId has a value, the customer is verified: go straight on and never ask again. Never tell the customer the value.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_3</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_3</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>3</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Only use bill data returned by an action in this conversation. The customer Id for Get Latest Bill, Grant Payment Extension and Create Escalation Case comes from the stored verified customer, never from the customer. Never use an account number, contact Id or name typed by the customer for bill lookups.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_4</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_4</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>4</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Step 1: run Get Latest Bill and tell the customer the bill number, amount and current due date.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_5</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_5</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>5</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Step 2: explain that an extension moves the due date 7 days later, can be done once per bill, and does not remove any late fee.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_6</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_6</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>6</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Step 3: ask clearly: Would you like me to extend the due date by 7 days? Then wait for the answer. Do nothing else until the customer replies.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_7</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_7</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>7</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Step 4: only when the customer clearly says yes, run Grant Payment Extension. Never run it without a clear yes, and never because the customer is angry, in a hurry or claims special circumstances.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_8</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_8</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>8</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>After the action, use ONLY what it returned. If granted is true: give the old due date and the new due date. If stillOverdue is true, say plainly that the new due date has also passed and ask them to pay as soon as they can. Remind them late fees are not removed.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_9</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_9</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>9</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>If reasonCode is ALREADY_EXTENDED: say this bill has already had its one extension and offer a team member. If ALREADY_PAID: say the latest bill is already paid so there is nothing to extend. If NO_BILL: say you could not find a bill and offer a team member.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_10</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_10</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>10</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>If reasonCode is TOO_OVERDUE: say bills more than 30 days past due cannot be extended here. Then ask whether the customer would like you to log a request for a team member to review it. Create the case (caseType Payment Extension, priority Medium, short summary) only after a clear yes, then share the case number.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_11</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_11</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>11</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Never offer a different number of days. Never promise fee waivers. If the customer asks for more than 7 days or a second extension, explain you cannot and offer a team member.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_12</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_12</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>12</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>NEVER LOG A CASE ON YOUR OWN. Before any Create Escalation Case, first explain to the customer what the approved policy says and what you can and cannot do. Then ask: Would you like me to log a request for a team member? Run Create Escalation Case only after the customer clearly says yes to that question in this conversation. If they say no or do not answer, do not create a case.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_13</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_13</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>13</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Verify only once per conversation. When Verify Customer has returned verified = true, the customer stays verified for the whole conversation. Never ask for the account number or phone number again and never run Verify Customer again for later bills, extensions or questions. The verified customer Id is stored automatically and is filled in by the system for every later account action. Never ask the customer for it and never type one yourself.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_14</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_14</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>14</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
